   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***The digestion of starch***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Proteases"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Proteases are a group of **enzymes that break down proteins into amino acids** in the stomach and small intestine (with the enzymes in the small intestine having been produced in the pancreas)"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/01/The-digestion-of-proteins.png",
   "file": "assets/4555322f522f-the-digestion-of-proteins.png",
   "alt": "The digestion of proteins, IGCSE & GCSE Biology revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***The digestion of proteins***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Lipases"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Lipase** enzymes are produced in the **pancreas** and secreted into the **duodenum**\n- They digest **lipids into fatty acids and glycerol**"
  },
